&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Product Design team is composed of several teams that work together to help define, create, and deliver all user-facing aspects of the Stripe brand and product. Product Design Managers work directly with Engineering leaders, Product Managers, Data Scientists, and Marketers in each product area. Together, they identify the strategy and vision, and drive execution for critical initiatives that create a world-class support experience for all Stripe customers and users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Global Payments builds on core Stripe financial products and creates solutions that empower businesses to expand into new markets worldwide without the friction of complex global operations. The sheer volume of payments that flow through Stripe on an hourly basis necessitates the highest level of craft and reliability, which means that Global Payments product designers have the chance to create and ship the best work of their careers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the leader of the Global Payments Design team, you will shape the products and experiences that make it as easy for businesses to sell globally as it is to sell locally. This team oversees product experiences around cross-border commerce, covering local payment methods, global tax compliance, localized consumer experiences, and moving money across borders. You&#39;ll ensure that any business can use Stripe to reach customers anywhere in the world, including fast-growing companies that expect to operate globally from day one.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll lead and grow a team of experienced designers who have a track record of navigating ambiguity and delivering high-impact solutions that improve payments experiences for Stripe users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage a growing, business-critical team of designers distributed across EMEA and APAC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expand the team to meet business demands and employee development needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Product Management leaders to identify, shape, and prioritize current and new product initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across Stripe teams and establish collaboration practices that result in holistic solutions for a horizontal product space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Product Management, Product Engineering, Marketing, and senior leadership to drive fast decision making, create clarity, and raise the bar for craft and impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspire, motivate, and lead designers across experience levels to do the best work of their careers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 5+ years of people management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 8+ years of relevant design experience at a tech or product-driven company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You excel at motivating and inspiring people to do their best work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience recruiting and building product design teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are relentlessly user-focused&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience designing for complex platforms and enterprise software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You excel at both written and spoken communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You do your best work collaboratively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You find a meaningful balance between speed, quality, and risky but interesting work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We design the products founders and finance teams use to understand their business and grow it. That spans two connected areas.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data Products covers analytics, database, and data pipeline. These are the surfaces where a business asks questions of its own Stripe data and gets answers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ecosystems and Startups covers Atlas, the App Marketplace, and the Business Network. These are how a company incorporates, connects to the tools around it, and transacts with other businesses on Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits at the intersection of building trust in the internet economy, platform design, and new product creation, making it one of the most strategically important design opportunities at Stripe. It’s a strong fit for a designer who is energized by ambiguity, motivated by impact, and excited to shape both shared systems used across Stripe and net-new products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of design experience at a tech, product-driven company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong portfolio demonstrating excellent craft, systems thinking, and end-to-end design, including a strong understanding of AI tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading complex product work in close partnership with product management engineering, and design leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shaping ambiguous spaces and driving clarity through design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of influencing cross-functional teams and product direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrive in environments where the opportunity spans systems, strategy, and zero to one product thinking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoy turning complex systems, policies, and edge cases into elegant product experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are energized by ambiguous, strategic problem spaces, not just well-defined execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are an influential storyteller who can align partners around a clear point of view&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can move fluidly between big-picture thinking and interaction-level craft&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Know how to build trust through design, especially in high-stakes or sensitive user moments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work well across disciplines and build credibility with technical, operational, and policy-oriented partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? At&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;, we are uncompromising on our mission to increase economic freedom. The bar is high, the environment is intense, and we like it that way. This isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits. If you&#39;re ready to build the future of finance alongside people who refuse to settle for &quot;good enough,&quot; you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for intense in-person working sessions called “surges.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers&quot;&gt;learn more about working at Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;The Design Systems team at Coinbase plays a critical role in executing on our vision to create more economic freedom for the world, and is at the center of execution for products across the entirety of the company. Join the Design Systems team within the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers/product-groups#pg-tabs&quot;&gt;Consumer &amp;amp; Business &lt;/a&gt;group as a Product Designer II and shape the foundation that powers every product Coinbase ships to millions of customers. This team owns the Coinbase Design System (CDS), the single system responsible for delivering quality, consistency, and trust at scale across every experience we build. You&#39;ll develop scalable components and patterns that help customers - from first-time crypto users to advanced traders - complete their tasks with ease and confidence, working closely with Design and Engineering across Platform and Consumer orgs to make the complex feel simple.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the iterative improvement of design system components and patterns, ensuring they scale across web and mobile products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive new system features from ideation through prototyping, user testing, and production delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Design and Engineering teams across the company to document, define, and evangelize scalable design patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead participation in design reviews, seeking specific feedback and incorporating relevant input to raise the quality bar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute on the design systems product roadmap and contribute to long-term systems strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of professional product design experience, including a focus specifically on design systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience designing scalable components and systems for consumer-facing web and mobile products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with AI design tools (e.g., Figma Make, Vercel V0, Cursor) applied to systems-level work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert-level Figma skills including prototyping design system components within product screens&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record collaborating cross-functionally with engineers, user researchers, and product teams to ship systems at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizes generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in workflow efficiency, cost, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Transparency Notice:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Base salary varies by location (see range below). Total compensation may also include equity and bonus eligibility, and benefits (medical, dental, vision, 401(k)).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
